import kotlin.Boolean;

-- Migration to v7: adds hasSeenOnboarding to `settings` (GAME_DESIGN.md §9h, first-time
-- onboarding). Defaults 0/false, matching Settings.sq's column default -- see 1.sqm's doc comment
-- for why this ships in the same commit as the column, not after (an already-installed device's
-- DB is only ever brought up to date by Schema.migrate(), which only runs when a .sqm file bumps
-- the schema version -- a column added without one crashes existing installs with "no such
-- column" the next time SettingsRepository reads/writes it).
--
-- Any device already installed before this migration lands on hasSeenOnboarding=false (the
-- column's DEFAULT), meaning it will see the onboarding experience once on its next launch even
-- though it isn't a genuinely first-ever install. This is accepted, not an oversight: there is no
-- "already onboarded" signal to backfill from for pre-existing installs (nothing tracked
-- first-launch before this flag existed), and false is the strictly safer default of the two --
-- an onboarding sequence a returning tester sees once more is a minor, one-time nuisance, whereas
-- defaulting true would silently skip onboarding for every genuinely-new player already counted
-- among "existing" rows at migration time, which is the actual failure this feature exists to
-- prevent.
ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN hasSeenOnboarding INTEGER AS Boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
